      <section class="section">
        <article class="feature-box">
          <p>AI tools are most useful when they turn scattered ideas into a structured plan. Instead of collecting destination notes in random lists, travelers can sort notes into categories like budget, logistics, attractions, food, and timing.</p>
          <p>That is where AI becomes genuinely helpful: it can summarize large quantities of research, highlight contradictions, and suggest a clearer route based on preferences and travel constraints.</p>
          <p>Still, travelers should validate recommendations using official sources, local guidance, and recent reviews before making bookings or setting strict itineraries.</p>
        </article>
